Members of the Welsh Assembly (AM) are concerned about “looking muppets”
Some Members of the Assembly are puzzled by the suggestion that their title should be changed to Members of the Welsh Parliament (MWP).
This bewilderment arises from the plans to change the name of the Assembly to Parliament of Wales.
Members of the Assembly from across the political spectrum are concerned that this could be ridiculed.
A Member of the Labour Party Assembly stated that his group was concerned “to rhyme with Twp and Pwp.”
For readers outside of Wales: In Welsh, tμp means silly and pwp means poop.
A member of the Welsh Party Assembly remarked that his entire group was “discontent” and has suggested alternatives.
A member of the Welsh Conservative Party claimed that his group was “open” to the name change, but noted that MWP’s jump to muppet was small.
In this context, the pronunciation of welsh lyrics is similar to that of Yorkshire lyrics or English.
The Committee of the Assembly, which currently draws up the legislation to introduce the name change, states: “Of course, the final decision on any descriptive element of the denomination of the Members of the Assembly shall be the matter of the members themselves.”
Welsh government’s 2017 law gave the Welsh Assembly the power to change its name.
In June, the Commission published the results of a public consultation of the proposals that revealed broad support to call the Welsh Parliament to the Assembly.
On the question of the title of the Members of the Assembly, the Commission preferred Members of the Welsh Parliament (or WMP), but the MWP option obtained most of the support in a public consultation.
Members of the Assembly are reportedly suggesting alternative options, but the struggle to reach a consensus could bring Assembly Speaker Elin Jones, who should sent the bill on changes in a few weeks.
Legislation on reforms will include other changes related to the functioning of the assembly, such as rules on the disqualification of Members of the Assembly and the design of the system of committees.
Members of the Assembly will have the final say in the question of what they should be called when they deliberate over legislation.
The Macedonians come to the polls to vote a referendum on the country’s name change
Voters will vote on Sunday on whether their country’s name will be changed to “Republic of North Macedonia.”
The popular vote was called in an attempt to resolve a decades-long conflict with the neighbouring country, Greece, which has its own province called Macedonia.
Athens has always insisted that the name of its northern neighbor represents a claim of its territory and has repeatedly opposed its candidacy for accession to the EU and NATO.
Macedonian President Gjorge Ivanov, who opposes the plebiscite on the name change, has said he will ignore the vote.
However, supporters of the referendum, including Prime Minister Zoran Zaev, contend that the name change is simply the price that must be paid to join the EU and NATO.
The bells of St. Martin are silent because of the difficulties of Harlem’s churches
“Historically, the older people I’ve talked to say that there was a bar and a church in every corner,” says Mr. Adams.
“Today, there isn’t one thing or the other.”
He pointed out that the disappearance of bars was understandable.
“Now people socialize differently,” he says.
“Bars are no longer the living rooms of the neighborhoods that neighbors go to regularly.”
Regarding the churches, he is concerned that the money obtained from the sale of goods will not last as long as the leaders expect and that “before or later, they will return to the starting point.”
Churches, he added, could be replaced by apartment buildings full of the kind of people who won’t help the sanctuaries left in the neighborhood.
“The vast majority of people who buy apartments in these buildings will be white people,” he said, “and, therefore, they will accelerate the closure of these churches, as it is unlikely that most of the people who move into these apartments will end up being members of these churches.”
The two churches were built by white congregations before Harlem became a black metropolis: the Metropolitan Community in 1870 and St. Martin a decade later.
The original white Methodist congregation left in the 30's of the 20th century.
A black congregation worshipping nearby acquired the building.
A black congregation took the reins of St. Martin, under the direction of Rev. John Howard Johnson, who led a boycott of 125th Street merchants, a main shopping street in Harlem, who were reluctant to hire or promote black people.
In 1939, a fire left the building severely damaged and, while Father Johnson’s parishioners made plans for its reconstruction, they also commissioned the carrion.
Reverend David Johnson, the son and successor of Father Johnson in St. Martin, proudly called him “the campaigns of the poor.”
In July, the expert who played the carillon called “a cultural treasure” and “an irreplaceable historical instrument.”
In addition, the expert, Tiffany Ng, of the University of Michigan, pointed out that it was the world’s first lanet used by a black musician, Dionisio A. Lind, who left to play Riverside Church’s longest-sized Riverside Church 18 years ago.
Mr. Merriweather remarked that St. Martin did not replace him.
What has happened in Saint Martin in recent months has been a complicated history of architects and contractors, some brought in by the lay leaders of the church and others by the episcopal Diocese.
The parish junta, the parish’s governing body, made up of lay leaders, wrote to the diocese in July commenting on its concern that the diocese “tried to pass the costs” to the board, although it had not participated in the hiring of architects and contractors sent by the diocese.
Some parishioners complained about the diocese’s lack of transparency.
Shark wounds 13-year-old boy drinking for lobsters in California
A shark attacked and injured a 13-year-old boy on Saturday while snorkeling for lobsters in California the day the locust season opened, according to authorities.
The attack occurred shortly before 7 a.m. near Beacon’s Beach in Encinitas.
Chad Hammel told San Diego’s KSWB-TV that he had been diving with friends for half an hour on Saturday morning when he heard the boy calling for help, so he approached a group to get him out of the water.
Hammel commented that, at first, he thought he was just excited to have captured a lobster, but then he realized that “he was screaming he had been bited
,
He had a shattered collarbone,” Hammel observed when he arrived next to the boy.
“I screamed at everyone to get out of the water because there was a shark,” Hammel added.
The boy was transported by helicopter to Rady Children Hospital, where he is in critical condition.
The shark species responsible for the attack is unknown.
The rescuer, Captain Larry Giles, told a news conference that a shark had been sighted in the area a few weeks earlier, but that it had not been considered a dangerous species.
Giles added that the victim showed traumatic injuries to the upper torso.
Authorities closed access to the beach, from Ponto Beach in Casablad to Swami Beach in Encinitas for 48 hours to investigate and for safety reasons.
Giles pointed out that there are more than 135 shark species in the area, but that most are not considered dangerous.
Sainsbury's plans boost UK beauty market
Sainsbury's acquires Boots, Superdrug and Debenhams, which have many employees specializing in the halls of their style and beauty establishments.
In order to significantly boost the UK beauty market, valued at 2800 trillion pounds and with increasing growth compared to falling sales in fashion and household appliances, larger beauty aisles will be tested in 11 stores across the country and, if successfully surpassed, the same will be done in more stores next year.
The investment in beauty comes at the same time that this supermarket chain is looking for ways to use shelf space that used to go to televisions, microwaves and household items.
Sainsbury's stated that it would double its beauty offer with up to 3000 products, including brands like Revlon, Essie, Tweezerman and Dr. PawPaw for the first time.
In addition, more space will be given to the existing ranges of L'Oreal, Maybelline and Burt's Bees, with areas similar to those of other establishments, such as Boots.
The chain will also relaunch its range of Boutique makeup with a majority of animal-friendly products, something increasingly demanded by younger customers.
The Fragrance Shop will also test its concessions at two Sainsbury’s establishments, the first recently opened in Croydon in South London last week. The second will open at Selly Oak in Birmingham later this year.
Online stores and the shift towards the daily purchase of small amounts of food in local stores force supermarkets to strive to convince people to visit them.
Mike Coupe, Sainsbury’s chief executive, has stated that stores will increasingly resemble shopping malls as the supermarket chain tries to fight discount stores Aldi and Lidl by offering more non-food services and products.
Sainsbury’s has integrated Argos discount outlets into hundreds of establishments and has introduced several Habitats since its purchase of these chains two years ago. It is considered that this has fueled grocency sales and made these acquisitions more profitable.
The supermarket chain’s previous attempt to renovate its beauty and pharmacy departments was a failure.
Sainsbury's tested a joint operation with Boots in the early 2000's, but the collaboration ended after a discussion on how to divide revenues from pharmaceutical outlets in their supermarkets.
The new strategy follows the sale of Sainsbury’s 281 pharmaceutical establishments to Celesio, owner of the Lloyds Pharmacy chain for 125 million pounds three years ago.
It is noted that Lloyds will participate in the plan, adding an expanded range of luxury skin care brands such as La Roche-Posay and Vichy in four stores.
Paul Mills-Hicks, Chief Commercial Officer of Sainsbury’s commented, “We’ve transformed the look and feel of our beauty aisles in a way that enhances the environment for our customers.
In addition, we have invested in a specialized staff that will be available to offer advice.
Our brand offering is designed to suit all needs. On the other hand, an attractive environment and a comfortable location makes us an irresistible destination for beauty products, defying the older way to buy.”
Peter Jones is “furious” after Holly Willoughby breaks an 11-million-pound deal
Dragon’s Den star Peter Jones left “furious” after TV host Holly Willoughby broke an 11-million-pound deal with her lifestyle business line to focus on her new contracts with Marks and Spencer and ITV.
Willoughby doesn’t have time to dedicate to Truly’s fashion and add-on brand.
This business had compared to Gwyneth Paltrow’s Goop brand.
The 37-year-old presenter of This Morning announced that she was leaving business on Instagram.
Holly Willoughby has enraged Dragon’s Den star Peter Jones by abandoning his lucrative last-minute lifestyle business to focus on his extraordinary new contracts with Marks & Spencer and ITV.
According to the sources consulted, Jones was “furious” when the golden girl of television admitted that her new agreements, valued at up to 1.5 million pounds, left no time to dedicate herself to Truly, its fashion brand and accessories, during a tense meeting held on Tuesday at the headquarters of her business empire in Marlow in Buckinghamshire.
The business had been compared to Gwyneth Paltrow’s Goop brand and was shaping up a favorite to double Willoughby’s 11-million-pound fortune.
While Willoughby, 37, announced that he was leaving business on Instagram, Jones was leaving Britain to go to one of his holiday homes.
“Truly was, by far, Holly’s top priority.
It was going to be her long-term future, which would keep her in the next two decades.
His decision to leave left everyone involved totally stunned.
No one could believe what happened on Tuesday, so close to launch.
There’s a warehouse full of merchandise at Marlow’s headquarters, ready-to-sell products.”
Experts believe the departure of the host of This Morning, one of Britain’s most profitable stars, could cost the company millions due to major investment in products ranging from cushions and sails to clothing, and possibly further delay its launch.
It could also mean an end to a long friendship.
Willoughby and her husband, Dan Baldwin, are the parents of three children and ten years ago maintain a close relationship with Jones and his wife, Tara Capp.
Willoughby established Truly with Capp in 2016 and Jones, 52, joined as president in March.
Couples went on vacation together and Jones has a 40% stake in Baldwin's television producer.
Willoughby is going to become brand ambassador for M&S and will replace Ant McPartlin as host of I'm A Celebrity on ITV.
A source close to Jones claimed that last night “there was no talk of business issues.”
A difficult conversation “and then we fell in love”
He was joking about the criticism he receives from the media for making a comment that some would consider “unpresidential” and for being so positive about the North Korean leader.
Why has President Trump resigned so many things?
Trump commented with his mocking voice of “news anchor.”
“I haven’t given up anything.”
He noted that Kim is interested to meet him again after Trump commended the first meeting held in June in Singapore, which he considered a major step towards the denuclearization of North Korea.
However, negotiations for denuclearisation have stalled.
More than three months after the June summit in Singapore, North Korea’s top diplomat Ri Yong Ho told world leaders gathered at the U.N. General Assembly on Saturday that his country does not see an “appropriate response” from the U.S
On the contrary, he said, the U.S. continues to apply sanctions in order to maintain pressure.
Trump’s perspective was much more optimistic in the speech he gave during his rally.
“We get along great with North Korea,” he said.
“We were going to go to war with North Korea.
Millions of people would have died.
Now we have a fantastic relationship.”
He said his efforts to improve relations with Kim have yielded positive results: an end to missile tests, aid to free hostages and bring the remains of U.S. soldiers back home.
In addition, he defended his unusual approach when talking about relations with Kim.
“It’s very easy to be presidential, but like that, instead of 10 000 people out there trying to get into this crowded stadium, we’d have about 200 people right here,” Trump said, pointing to the people right in front of him.
A tsunami and an earthquake in Indonesia devastate an island, leaving hundreds dead
After the Lombok earthquake, for example, foreign non-governmental organizations were informed that their assistance was not required.
Although more than 10% of Lombok’s population had had to move, no national emergency was declared, a prerequisite for catalysing international aid.
