The death toll from the Indonesian tsunami rises to 832
The number of casualties from the earthquake and tsunami in Indonesia has risen to 832, as reported by the country’s emergency agency early Sunday.
Many people were trapped in the rubble of buildings that collapsed during Friday’s 7.5-magnitude quake that unleashed waves of up to six meters, agency spokesman Sutopo Purwo Nugroho said during a news conference.
The city of Palu, with more than 380 000 inhabitants, was covered with the remains of the collapsed buildings.
Police arrest a 32-year-old man on suspicion of murder after a woman was stabbed to death
An investigation has been opened for murder after the body of a woman in Birkenhead in Merseyside this morning has opened.
The 44-year-old woman was found at 7:55 with stab wounds at Grayson Mews on John Street, marking the arrest of a 32-year-old man on suspicion of murder.
Police have urged people in the area to see or hear anything to come to the police.
Inspector Brian O'Hagan said, “The investigation is in the early stages, but it would encourage anyone who was near Jonh Street in Birkenhead and have seen or heard something suspicious to contact us.
In addition, I would advise anyone, especially taxi drivers, to have been able to capture something on dashcam to contact us as they may have vital information for our research.”
A police spokesman has confirmed that the woman whose body has been found is from Birkenhead and found inside a property.
This afternoon some people who believe they met the woman arrived at the scene of the crime to know where she had been found this morning.
The investigation is ongoing and the police have reported that they are in the process of informing the victim’s relatives.
A taxi driver living in Grayson Mews has tried to re-enter his apartment, but the police tell him that no one can enter or leave the building.
He was perplexed when he discovered what had happened.
Now, residents are informed that they will be allowed to re-enter in a few hours.
Someone heard an officer tell a man that the whole area was being treated as a crime scene.
A woman appeared at the place in tears.
He keeps repeating “it’s terrible.”
At two o’clock in the afternoon, there were two police vans inside the cordon and one more outside.
