That game continued until the second half, although Alfredo Morelos forced a stop by Kelly.
Allan McGregor, the Rangers' goalkeeper turned down Scott Pittman's one-way shot, and Lithgow was far from another of the Livingston.
Long passes entered in the Livingston area, but they were always clear. Two penalty petitions were rejected, one after a Halkett inning over backup Glenn Middleton and another for a hand.
