Alasdair Lamont from BBC Scotland at Tony Macaroni Stadium
A phenomenal performance and result for the Livingston.
The unanimous opinion is that they made an excellent game that continued to exceed expectations of an upward trajectory.
His style of play and squad have barely undergone any changes since his promotion, but this is largely due to Holt because of the way he has reinforced the team since his arrival.
He had a lot of heroes.
Halkett, the captain of the team, was huge and led a magnificently organized defense, while Menga kept Connor Goldson and Joe Worrall alert at all times.
The Rangers lacked inspiration, though.
