“We’re going to mobilise this country’s people’s military that gave us victory with Brexit and we’ll never rest until we’ve become an independent, self-driving and proud UK.”
In the meantime, those in favor of staying toured the streets of Birmingham before the two-hour rally in the city center.
Some activists waved Tories Against Brexit banners following the group's presentation this weekend.
Labour’s Lord Adonis mocked the Conservatives for the security issues they had with an application of the party during the opening of the conference.
“These are the same people who tell us that they can implement computer systems and all the technology for Canada Plus Plus, for borders in harmony, for free trading without borders in Ireland.”
“It’s a total farce.
There is nothing that can be considered a good Brexit,” he added.
