The U.S. Navy said sailors who were carrying out dock-enhancing jobs nearby also assisted in the rescue using an inflatable boat to transport people ashore before the plane sank about 30 meters (100 feet) underwater.
Data from the aviation safety network indicate that 111 people have died in airline accidents registered in Papua New Guinea over the past two decades, but none with Air Niugini.
