Another black person?
New York nanny sues couple for firing her after “racist” text
A New York nanny is going to sue a partner for discriminatory dismissal after mistakenly receiving a text message from the mother complaining she was “another black person.”
The couple denies that it is racist and compares the lawsuit to an “extortion” case.
Lynsey Plasco-Flaxman, a mother of two, expressed her dismay at the discovery that the new child caregiver, Giselle Maurice, was black when she arrived on her first day of work in 2016.
