Mourning women put cards to avoid suicides is a bridge
Two women who lost loved ones because of suicides are working to prevent others from taking their own lives.
Sharon Davis and Kelly Humphreys have been putting cards on a Welsh bridge with inspiring messages and phone numbers that people can call for help.
Tyler, Mrs. Davis' son, was 13 when he began suffering from depression and committed suicide at the age of 18.
“I don’t want any parent to feel what I feel every day,” he said.
Davis, a 45-year-old who lives in Lydney, said his son was a promising chef with a contagious smile.
