U.S.-China trade war could benefit Beijing
The first salvos of the U.S.-China trade war were deafening, and while there is still much left for the battle to end, a rift between countries could benefit Beijing, experts say.
U.S. President Donald Trump issued the first warning earlier this year by placing tariffs on major Chinese exports, such as solar panels, steel and aluminum.
Significant escalation took place this week with new tariffs affecting 200,000 million dollars (150,000 million pounds) in products, which carries taxes on half of the products entering the United States from China.
On all occasions, Beijing has retaliated equivalently, recently enforcing five-to-ten-percent tariffs on U.S. products worth US$60,000 million.
