Achieving that Washington retreat would mean ceding to lawsuits, but publicly submitting to the U.S. it would be too embarrassing for Chinese President Xi Jinping.
Still, experts say that if Beijing plays its cards well, pressures from the U.S. trade war could positively help China in the long term by reducing interdependence between the two economies.
“The fact that a swift political decision in Washington or Beijing can make conditions to start a plummeting of the economy in either country is actually much more dangerous than viewers have recognized so far,” said Abigail Grace, Asia-focused associate researcher for the Strategic Cabinet Center for New American Security.
Syria is ready for refugees to return, Foreign Minister says
Syria says it is ready for the voluntary return of refugees and asks for help to rebuild a country devastated by a war that has been more than seven years.
In a speech earlier by the United Nations General Assembly, Foreign Minister Walid al-Moualem said the country’s conditions were improving.
“The situation on the ground today is more stable and secure thanks to the progress that has been made in the fight against terrorism,” he said.
The government continues to rehabilitate areas destroyed by terrorists to try to restore normalcy.
There are already all the conditions for the voluntary return to the country of the refugees who had to abandon it due to terrorism and the unilateral economic measures that affected their daily lives and their livelihoods.
The U.N. estimates that, since the war began in 2011, more than 5.5 million Syrians have fled the country.
There are another six million people still living in the country who need humanitarian aid.
Al-Moualem acknowledged that the Syrian regime would appreciate the aid to rebuild the devastated country.
But he also stressed that he would not accept conditional aid or help from countries that promoted the insurgency.
Europe takes the Ryder Cup in Paris
The European team has won the 2018 Ryder Cup by defeating the U.S. team with a 16.5 to 10.5 final score at Le Golf National, just outside Paris (France).
The U.S. has now had six consecutive defeats on European soil since the last time it won a Ryder Cup in Europe in 1993.
Europe regained the crown when Danish captain Thomas Bjorn’s team scored the 14.5 points needed to beat the United States.
The American star Phil Mickelson, who had to fight during most of the tournament, pitched his starting point on the hole 16 par 3, thus admitting his loss to Francesco Molinari.
Italian golfer Molinari excelled in all of his rounds, becoming one of four players who have never achieved a 5-0-0 since the current tournament format began in 1979.
Jordan Spieth was defeated by 5 and 4 against the player with the lowest classification of the European team, the Danish Thorbjorn Olesen.
The world’s number one player, Dustin Johnson, fell 2 and 1 to England’s Ian Poulter, who could have played his last Ryder Cup.
Sergio Garcia, a veteran who already has eight Ryder Cups, became the European with the most victories of the tournament of all time, with 25.5 points in his career.
“I don’t usually cry, but I can’t help it today.
It's been a very tough year.
I am totally grateful to Thomas for choosing and believing in me.
I'm very, very happy that I was able to recover the cup.
It’s an achievement of the whole team and I’m very happy to have been able to help,” said an excited Garcia after the European team’s victory.
Now his compatriot John Rahm’s torch, who already defeated American golf legend Tiger Woods by 2 and 1 in a singles match on Sunday.
“I’m incredibly proud to have beaten Tiger Woods as I’ve grown up seeing this man,” said 23-year-old golfer John Rahm.
Woods lost all four games in France and now has a 13-21-3 record in his Ryder Cup career.
This is a strange statistic for one of the greatest players of all time, who has won 14 great titles, falling behind only Jack Nicklaus.
The U.S. team had to fight throughout the weekend to find the streets, with the exception of Patrick Reed, Justin Thomas and Tony Finau, who played high-level golf throughout the tournament.
